    "abstract": "Parts figure for the centre tank boost pump and the sump items around it, covering the restrictors, the ducting, the collars and the local shell doubler at the belly fairing penetration.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the boost pump installation items in the centre tank sump, including the restrictors that set the motive flow and the items at the tank boundary penetration.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the sump looking aft with the pump withdrawn. Items 10 and 20 set the motive flow balance and must be changed as a pair; a mismatched pair will hold delivery pressure but will not sweep the shallow region forward of the low point. Item 30 is deleted on aircraft that have the water scavenge installed. Item 60 appears only where the scavenge line crosses the shell into the aft belly fairing."
    },
